Group design image + CutContour into one Illustrator group in contour PDF

Task: User asked that the image and the CutContour in the contour download be
"grouped" — specifically as one selectable group in Illustrator (art + cut line
move/select together).

Change (client/src/lib/contour-outline.ts, downloadContourPDF):
- Instead of drawing the bleed background and design raster directly on the page
  and appending the cut path(s) as separate page content streams, all of these
  (bg image, design image, active CutContour path, optional locked contour path)
  are now accumulated into a single PDF Form XObject (Type/XObject, Subtype/Form,
  BBox = full page). Illustrator imports a Form XObject as one Group.
- The CutContour Separation color spaces now live in the form's own Resources
  (not page-level). The form is registered as /ArtCutGroup in page XObject
  resources and drawn once via "q /ArtCutGroup Do Q".
- Removed the two page.drawImage() calls; images are referenced by ref inside the
  form resources (still embedded at save via embedPng).
- Vector QR overlay moved to run AFTER the form draw so QR modules stay on top
  (z-order preserved). Spot-color white/gloss layers remain separate page layers
  (production separations, intentionally not part of the art group).
- Added PDFRef import; added guards so page Resources/Contents are created when
  absent (previously created implicitly by drawImage).

Scope: only downloadContourPDF. generateContourPDFBase64, shape-outline.ts, and
gang-sheet.ts export paths are unchanged.

Verification: type-check shows no new errors in contour-outline.ts (pre-existing
unrelated errors remain); app runs clean (no console/runtime errors); architect
code review passed with no blocking issues. Non-blocking note: naive preflight
tools that scan only page-level ColorSpace may not list the spot plate since it
is now nested in the form — RIP rendering is unaffected.

Also (earlier this session): answered that CutContour is a STROKE (S operator,
0.5pt, Separation color) while white/gloss spot colors are FILLS (f* even-odd);
confirmed the prior Sharp enhance-image route work was already in place.
